### Document Service Tests - Using Nginx Reverse Proxy
### These tests use the nginx reverse proxy routes (port 80) instead of direct service ports

@baseUrl = http://localhost/api

### 1. Upload document for internship application
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary123
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="application_id"

APPLICATION_ID_HERE
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="document_type"

cv
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="cv.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

[Binary PDF content would go here - use a real file in actual testing]
--boundary123--

### 2. Upload motivation letter
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary123
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="application_id"

APPLICATION_ID_HERE
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="document_type"

motivation_letter
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="motivation.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

[Binary PDF content would go here]
--boundary123--

### 3. Upload academic transcript
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary123
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="application_id"

APPLICATION_ID_HERE
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="document_type"

academic_transcript
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="transcript.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

[Binary PDF content would go here]
--boundary123--

### 4. Get all documents for a specific application
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents?application_id=APPLICATION_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### 5. Get specific document by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/DOCUMENT_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### 6. Test file download through nginx storage route
### This should return a download URL that works through nginx reverse proxy
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents/DOCUMENT_ID_HERE/download
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### 7. Test direct file access through nginx storage proxy
### Use the download URL returned from the previous request
GET http://localhost/storage/documents/FILENAME_HERE

### 8. List all documents (admin only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/documents
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ADMIN_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### 9. Upload with invalid application ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary123
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="application_id"

invalid-uuid
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="document_type"

cv
--boundary123
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

[Binary content]
--boundary123--

### 10. Upload with missing application ID
POST {{baseUrl}}/documents
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary123
